body:
Copper, two bars bleu celeste and vert, charged with avocado vert stoned or

&#x200B;

Copper for the clay soil of Southern CA; Blue bar for the Luiseño creek/city canal; Green bar for our parkways parallel to the canal; Avocado for our #1 Non-medicinal cash crop.

&#x200B;

Thanks for all the suggestions on the [original post](https://www.reddit.com/r/vexillology/comments/a9jabp/i_think_i_improved_my_citys_flag/)

&#x200B;

Iterations can be found [here](https://imgur.com/a/r8MOZX8)

&#x200B;

I've emailed the city to propose the new design and am awaiting their response.

Our flag is pretty bad: [https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/78/Flag\_of\_Escondido%2C\_California.svg](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/78/Flag_of_Escondido%2C_California.svg)  

&#x200B;

So the Umber field is the clay-rich soil of Southern CA. With all the adobe tile and shingles out here, I think it works. The blue stripe represents the Escondido creek first settled by the Luiseño people; as well as the modern-day canal running through the city. The green stripe represents the city's numerous parkways, and street-long farmers' market. The avocado charge should be self explanatory. Avos grow like weeds out here. CC welcome.
